---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Agentic platform operations — xnoto.dev"
  description="A source-backed framing for repeatable, tool-scoped agent workflows with human approval."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Reference framing</p>
    <h1>Agentic platform operations</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Repeatable agent environments are useful when they make work inspectable: a bounded task,
      approved tools, validation, recorded evidence, and a human decision where change matters.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="workflow">
    <h2 id="workflow">The workflow</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card"><h3>1. Bound the task</h3><p>State the objective, authoritative sources, exclusions, and expected output before delegation.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>2. Scope the tools</h3><p>Give an agent only the tools and access path its task needs; preserve the owning system’s controls.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>3. Validate evidence</h3><p>Separate authored source, CI validation, selected desired state, and verified runtime behavior.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>4. Keep approval human</h3><p>Use explicit approval gates for merges, publication, deployment, and live mutation.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="boundaries">
    <h2 id="boundaries">What this does not claim</h2>
    <p class="note">
      This page is an architecture framing, not a claim of a public production fleet, scale, availability,
      customer adoption, or autonomous operations. Those claims need separate, safe-to-publish evidence.
    </p>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>No unrestricted shell or cloud-control access by default.</li>
      <li>No credentials, state, or raw operational logs in public content.</li>
      <li>No autonomous production mutation without explicit human approval.</li>
      <li>No substitution of source evidence for runtime verification.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="public-evidence">
    <h2 id="public-evidence">Public evidence trail</h2>
    <p>
      The companion project index links public repositories and describes their status. The intent is to make
      implementation decisions and boundaries easier to inspect—not to turn a tool list into a marketing claim.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
